From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:30:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/18] openjpeg: Add an abort handler that stops a running
 decode.

opj_set_abort_handler() sets a callback that the decoder asks before
each code-block, between the wavelet, colour transform and level shift
steps, and every few rows inside them. When it returns true the decode
fails, so a caller can stop decoding a very large image early. Without
a handler nothing changes. The new symbols are renamed like the others
in opj_config.h.

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
